% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `bounded_channel`, compiled by
% psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  The class text is PRINTED
% SOURCE, not ours: TM-100 Figure 3.10 "Class 'bounded_channel'" (PDF
% p17, printed folio 15), as transcribed in
% docs/simpos/printed/listings/tm0100_p17.esp, verbatim (layout as
% printed).  Unlike Figs. 3.6-3.8 the caption does not say "part of".
% The plain `attribute post_queue;` overrides channel's slot of the same
% name and its initialiser (TM-100 p16 prose: "The slot 'post_queue' in
% class 'bounded_channel' contains a bounded post queue instead of a post
% queue by overriding the slot of class 'channel'"); create/3 then fills
% it.  No held program or package sends to it: it is here because it is
% printed.

    class  bounded_channel  has

    % PRINTED: TM-100 Fig. 3.10, PDF p17 (the nature)
    nature      channel;

    % PRINTED: TM-100 Fig. 3.10, PDF p17
    :create(Class, Channel, Limit) :-
            :create(Class, Channel),
            :create(#bounded_post_queue, Queue, Limit),
            Channel!post_queue := Queue;

    instance

    % PRINTED: TM-100 Fig. 3.10, PDF p17 (the overriding slot)
    attribute   post_queue;

    end.
